<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · religion</p><h1 class="enc-title">Etruscan religion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900 BCE – c. 100 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Etruscan religion was the polytheistic belief and practice of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/etruscans">Etruscans</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, from the Villanovan period. It centred on seers’ revelations, sacred books and divination by entrails, thunder and lightning, and is known only from archaeology and Roman writers.</p></div>
